<file path="README.md">
# Xplore Labs

Teaching games for the Club ILISI platform **Xplore**. Students learn real technical skills by playing short missions, and their progress is saved to their Xplore account.

The first game teaches **Linux**: you type real commands in a simulated terminal to escape a locked server, helped by a penguin guide. Working title: **Root Escape**.

> **Status:** planning done, development not started yet. The full spec is in [`docs/PRD.md`](docs/PRD.md).

## Games

| Game | Guide | Status |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Linux (Root Escape) | Penguin | In design |
| SQL | Dolphin | Planned |
| Git | TBD | Planned |
| Networking | TBD | Planned |

## How it works

- A standalone **Next.js** app, served later at `/labs` on the Xplore domain (Next.js Multi-Zones).
- A **command engine** in TypeScript: virtual file system, parser (quotes, pipes, `>`, `>>`), interpreter and goal checker. It runs fully in the browser.
- **Missions** are written in YAML and validated with Zod at build time.
- The game talks to Xplore only through a **bridge**:
  - `mock`: saves progress in `localStorage` (used during development)
  - `api`: calls the `labs` module in the Xplore NestJS backend (added at integration)
- Points and stickers are given only by the server.

## Tech stack

| Area | Tools |
| --- | --- |
| App | Next.js (App Router), React, TypeScript |
| Terminal | xterm.js |
| Live folder map | D3.js |
| Characters and effects | Rive, GSAP, canvas-confetti |
| Sound | Howler.js |
| State | Zustand |
| Styling | Games: CSS modules, CSS variables, augmented-ui. Website pages: Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui, 8bitcn accents |
| Content | YAML + Zod |
| Tests | Vitest (engine), Playwright (missions) |
| Backend (later) | NestJS `labs` module in Xplore |

## Project structure (planned)

```text
xplore-labs/
  docs/PRD.md          full product spec
  public/intro/        Labs intro video (sound + silent)
  app/(site)/          website pages: hub, game details, mission map (navbar, Tailwind + shadcn)
  app/linux/           game screens: title screen, missions
  src/shared/          bridge, progress, sound, memes, UI, theme, game registry
  src/games/linux/     engine, mission content, UI, theme
  public/games/linux/  memes, sounds, characters, cover (capsule art)
  public/brand/        Xplore Labs logo and mark
  design/              source art (map islands), not deployed
  tests/               Vitest and Playwright tests
```

## Getting started

The app is not built yet. Once it is:

```bash
npm install
cp .env.example .env.local   # NEXT_PUBLIC_LABS_BRIDGE=mock
npm run dev                  # http://localhost:3000/labs
npm test                     # engine unit tests
```

## Environment variables

| Name | Used by | Value |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_LABS_BRIDGE` | game | `mock` now, `api` at integration |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_LABS_API_URL` | game | Xplore NestJS URL |
| `LABS_HMAC_SECRET` | NestJS only | long random string, never in the frontend |
| `GITHUB_TOKEN` | footer (server, optional) | read-only token ("Metadata: read" on this repo): lists the repo's contributors as developers. Without it the footer shows a fallback list |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_FEEDBACK_URL` | footer (optional) | where the "Your feedback" button leads; the button is hidden while it is empty |

## Roadmap

1. **Phase A:** build the full Linux game in mock mode (engine, missions 1 to 10, game screen, title screen, hub).
2. **Phase B:** add the `labs` module to the Xplore backend and connect the game.
3. **Later:** more games (SQL, Git, networking) using the same format.

See section 15 of the PRD for details.

## Contributing

- Read [`docs/PRD.md`](docs/PRD.md) before starting.
- Work on a branch and open a pull request into `main`.
- No copyrighted assets: use your own or free-to-use art, memes and sounds.
- Keep secrets out of the frontend and out of the repo.

## Team

- **Ali Zouhdi** ([@Ali-Dev06](https://github.com/Ali-Dev06))
- Second developer: TBD
- Built for the Club ILISI, FST Mohammedia.
</file>

<file path="src/games/linux/content/schema.ts">
import { z } from 'zod';
import type { Goal } from '../engine/goals';
import type { FsEntrySpec } from '../engine/vfs/spec';
import { ZONE_IDS } from '../meta';

/** Placeholders a mission may use. The bridge gives one personal password per mission. */
export const SECRET_NAMES = ['password'] as const;

export const localizedText = z.union([
  z.string().min(1),
  z.object({ en: z.string().min(1), fr: z.string().min(1).optional() }).strict(),
]);

export const MOODS = [
  'neutral',
  'happy',
  'thinking',
  'shocked',
  'proud',
  'disappointed',
  'laughing',
  'sleeping',
] as const;
export const mood = z.enum(MOODS);

export const dialogueLine = z.object({ mood, text: localizedText }).strict();

/** One line of a mission recap: a command taught, what it does, an example. */
export const recapEntry = z
  .object({
    command: z.string().min(1),
    text: localizedText,
    example: z.string().min(1).optional(),
  })
  .strict();

/** YAML reads `mode: 600` as a number, so both forms are accepted. */
const mode = z
  .union([z.string(), z.number().int()])
  .transform(String)
  .pipe(z.string().regex(/^[0-7]{3,4}$/, 'must be octal permissions like 644 or 0600'));

const userName = z.string().regex(/^[a-z_][a-z0-9_-]*$/, 'must be a Linux user name');
const entryName = z
  .string()
  .regex(/^[^/]+$/, 'must not contain /')
  .refine((name) => name !== '.' && name !== '..', 'cannot be . or ..');
const absolutePath = z.string().regex(/^\//, 'must start with /');

const fileEntry = z
  .object({
    type: z.literal('file').optional(),
    content: z.string(),
    mode: mode.optional(),
    owner: userName.optional(),
    group: userName.optional(),
  })
  .strict();

export const fsEntry: z.ZodType<FsEntrySpec> = z.lazy(() =>
  z.union([
    z.string(),
    z
      .object({
        type: z.literal('dir'),
        mode: mode.optional(),
        owner: userName.optional(),
        group: userName.optional(),
        children: z.record(entryName, fsEntry).optional(),
      })
      .strict(),
    fileEntry,
  ]),
);

export const goal: z.ZodType<Goal> = z.lazy(() =>
  z.discriminatedUnion('type', [
    z.object({ type: z.literal('password'), value: z.string().min(1) }).strict(),
    z
      .object({
        type: z.literal('file_exists'),
        path: z.string().min(1),
        nodeType: z.enum(['file', 'dir']).optional(),
      })
      .strict(),
    z.object({ type: z.literal('file_absent'), path: z.string().min(1) }).strict(),
    z
      .object({
        type: z.literal('file_content'),
        path: z.string().min(1),
        equals: z.string().optional(),
        contains: z.string().optional(),
      })
      .strict()
      .refine((g) => g.equals !== undefined || g.contains !== undefined, {
        message: 'file_content needs equals or contains',
      }),
    z.object({ type: z.literal('cwd'), path: z.string().min(1) }).strict(),
    z
      .object({
        type: z.literal('permission'),
        path: z.string().min(1),
        mode: mode,
      })
      .strict(),
    z
      .object({
        type: z.literal('command_used'),
        name: z.string().min(1).optional(),
        minPipeLength: z.number().int().min(1).optional(),
      })
      .strict(),
    z.object({ type: z.literal('all'), goals: z.array(goal).min(2) }).strict(),
  ]),
);

export const missionSchema = z
  .object({
    /** Stable id, also the file name. Used in the database: never rename a published mission. */
    id: z
      .string()
      .regex(/^[a-z0-9]+(-[a-z0-9]+)*$/, 'must be kebab-case, e.g. archive-hidden-scroll'),
    game: z.literal('linux').default('linux'),
    zone: z.enum(ZONE_IDS),
    /** Position in the campaign (1 to 10, bonus cases after). */
    order: z.number().int().positive(),
    title: localizedText,
    /** The goal in one short line, shown in the top bar. */
    objective: localizedText,
    guide: z.literal('penguin').default('penguin'),
    user: userName.refine((name) => name !== 'root', 'the player is never root').default('intern'),
    briefing: z.array(dialogueLine).min(1),
    filesystem: z.record(absolutePath, z.record(entryName, fsEntry)),
    start_dir: z.string().default('~'),
    goal,
    /** From vague to precise. The last one can give the answer. */
    hints: z.array(localizedText).min(1),
    /** Mission-specific reactions. `on` is a command line, matched after trimming. */
    reactions: z
      .array(z.object({ on: z.string().min(1), mood, text: localizedText }).strict())
      .default([]),
    victory: z.array(dialogueLine).min(1),
    rewards: z
      .object({ points: z.number().int().min(0), no_hint_bonus: z.number().int().min(0) })
      .strict(),
    /** Shown after the victory: the concept learned, in one sentence. */
    concept: localizedText,
    /** "What you learned" in the mission map's recap, unlocked once the mission is done. */
    recap: z.array(recapEntry).min(1),
    /** Commands that solve the mission. Checked at build time, shown when the player gives up. */
    solution: z.array(z.string().min(1)).min(1),
  })
  .strict();

export type Mission = z.output<typeof missionSchema>;
export type Mood = z.output<typeof mood>;
export type DialogueLine = z.output<typeof dialogueLine>;

/** Classic mistakes the guide reacts to (content/reactions.yaml). */
export const REACTION_KEYS = [
  'rm_rf_root',
  'sudo',
  'sudo_spam',
  'sl',
  'vim_trap',
  'cd_into_file',
  'permission_denied',
  'exit',
  'error_streak',
  'idle',
] as const;
export type ReactionKey = (typeof REACTION_KEYS)[number];

const reaction = z
  .object({ lines: z.array(dialogueLine).min(1), lesson: dialogueLine.optional() })
  .strict();

export const reactionsSchema = z
  .object({
    reactions: z.object(Object.fromEntries(REACTION_KEYS.map((key) => [key, reaction]))).strict(),
    unknown_command: z.object({ lines: z.array(dialogueLine).min(1), tip: dialogueLine }).strict(),
  })
  .strict();

export type Reaction = z.output<typeof reaction>;
export interface Reactions {
  reactions: Record<ReactionKey, Reaction>;
  unknown_command: { lines: DialogueLine[]; tip: DialogueLine };
}

/** Meme events (PRD section 7). */
export const MEME_EVENTS = [
  'give_up',
  'rm_rf_root',
  'sudo_spam',
  'vim_trap',
  'mission_success_no_hint',
  'idle_60s',
] as const;
export type MemeEvent = (typeof MEME_EVENTS)[number];

const assetPath = z
  .string()
  .regex(/^[\w./-]+\.(wav|mp3|ogg|png|svg|webp|gif)$/, 'must be a file path like sounds/x.mp3');

export const memesSchema = z.array(
  z
    .object({
      event: z.enum(MEME_EVENTS),
      sound: assetPath.optional(),
      sticker: assetPath.optional(),
      chance: z.number().min(0).max(1).default(1),
    })
    .strict()
    .refine((meme) => meme.sound || meme.sticker, 'a meme needs a sound or a sticker'),
);
export type Meme = z.output<typeof memesSchema>[number];

export interface LinuxContent {
  /** Sorted by `order`. */
  missions: Mission[];
  reactions: Reactions;
  memes: Meme[];
  /** "More info" text of the game details page (Markdown), per language. */
  about: { en: string; fr: string };
}
</file>

